  //
  // When `true`, this Team row is the user's auto-bootstrapped
  // personal workspace. The platform-context builder treats it as
  // `scope: "PERSONAL"` and `flags.isPersonalWorkspace: true`. A
  // partial unique index (see migration
  // `20260720100000_personal_workspace_bootstrap`) enforces AT MOST
  // ONE personal team per owner so the bootstrap is concurrency-safe.
  //
  // Defaults to `false` — all existing teams are TEAM-scoped.
  isPersonal Boolean @default(false) @map("is_personal")

  // P1 DOMAIN REMEDIATION (2026-07-21) — EXPLICIT workspace-kind
  // discriminator. `isPersonal=false` is NOT a valid "Organization
  // workspace" signal: self-service PRO/TEAM owned workspaces are also
  // isPersonal=false. The canonical classification is:
  //
  //   PERSONAL     — the owner's bootstrap Personal Space (isPersonal=true)
  //   OWNED        — a self-service user-owned workspace (FREE/PRO/TEAM)
  //   ORGANIZATION — an enterprise-organization operational workspace
  //
  // Nullable during rollout; the backfill migration classifies existing
  // rows deterministically (isPersonal→PERSONAL, ENTERPRISE plan→
  // ORGANIZATION, else OWNED). Readers must FAIL CLOSED on NULL when
  // presenting switch targets. Creation paths always set it explicitly.
  /**
   * PHASE 12 CORRECTIVE PASS §5.2 (ARCH-002, 2026-08-06) — MANDATORY.
   *
   * Nullable meant readers could not rely on it, which is why
   * `normalizeWorkspaceKind` carried a plan-derived fallback that turned a
   * commercial upgrade into a silent tenancy change. Made NOT NULL by
   * 20271125000000 after a backfill that classifies from STRUCTURAL authority
   * only (personal-space invariant, CUSTOMER-organization provisioning,
   * SYSTEM-container ownership) and refuses anything ambiguous.
   */
  workspaceKind WorkspaceKind @map("workspace_kind")

  // Phase 2.7X Stage 1 — nullable Organization FK.
  //
  // Phase 1 of the staged Organization migration: this column is
  // additive + nullable. Every existing Team has organizationId =
  // NULL until the Stage 2 backfill creates a 1:1 implicit
  // Organization per Team. No runtime code reads this column yet;
  // Stage 3 (dual-read endpoints) will start consuming it.
  //
  // The FK uses `onDelete: SetNull` so deleting an Organization
  // does NOT cascade-delete the Team's evidence — the Team
  // detaches from its org and continues to operate. Workspace
  // isolation guarantee survives org-row deletion.
  // Phase 2.7X Stage 6 — NOT NULL: every team is bound to an org.
  // FK semantics: Restrict — org deletion is refused while teams
  // remain bound. Operators must relocate teams first.
  organizationId String       @map("organization_id") @db.Uuid
  organization   Organization @relation("OrganizationToTeam", fields: [organizationId], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict)

  invites                   TeamInvite[]
  members                   TeamMember[]
  activities                TeamActivity[]
  payments                  Payment[]
  subscriptions             Subscription[]
